    "reading": {
        "body": "Five open developer relations roles in this sample sit at four companies, and two of them are the same Databricks title in two cities. That is a narrow slice of the AI labor market, not a measure of it.\n\nThe pattern is that the companies hiring for this function are infrastructure and platform vendors: Lambda, SambaNova, Databricks. Developer relations is a demand-generation role, so it tracks firms that need outside developers to build on their compute or their data platform. The Air Force Academy posting is the outlier, an academic appointment rather than a vendor job, and it is the only listing with a published salary.\n\nWhat this does not tell you is volume, trend, or pay for the category. Five postings over roughly seven weeks cannot establish a rate, and four of the five carry no compensation data. The sources listed include aggregators and a posting-share tracker, but none of their aggregate figures appear here, so nothing on this page supports a claim about whether AI hiring is rising or falling.\n\nThe connection to compute and power is indirect at best. Lambda and SambaNova sell compute, so their developer-facing hiring is downstream of capacity they have already built. Nothing here reports data centers, megawatts, or grid constraints, and the data should not be read as evidence about them.",
